                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fun and entertaining game to kill small amounts of time, I'll list the pros and cons below.\n\nPros:\n+ Fun gameplay\n+ Fell in love with the backgrounds (especially the night-time one)\n+ Different waves with different types of enemies make you want to continue playing\n+ Specials are completely different, and choosing them right according to your playstyle is very important\n+ Awesome soundtrack\n\nCons:\n- Specials are not entirely balanced (could be due to my playstyle though)\n- Lacks a tutorial, so I'll give some tips on that\n- Can't get past wave 7\n- Darn birds\n\nTips:\nx Roll! you can finish off stunned zombies by rolling in and out of them.\nx Max health is very strong compared to max ammo IMO\nx If you die, only use a revive if you aren't trying to reach your highscore. \n\nConclusion:\nDon't expect this Forest Warrior to be a game that can be played hours after hours, it's fun to fill in small amounts of time. I often play this while watching a stream or Netflix on my second screen. Although my steam says I haven't played it for that long, it had a free demo on kickstarter (you could play untill wave 4, which took me a long time to reach) which I played for approximatly 3 hours before it got released.\nIn my opinion this game is already worth the price of 3 euros, and it's still developing!\n\nPS bear in mind that this game is still in beta\nPPS if you can beat my highscore of 217069 I'll give you a cookie\n",
